---
import BaseEn from '../../layouts/BaseEn.astro';
---
<BaseEn title="Terms — OneTech Solutions" description="Terms of working with OneTech Solutions: the written offer is the basis, payment and subscription terms, third-party costs, and limits of responsibility.">

	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="eyebrow">Terms</div>
			<h1>Terms of working together</h1>
			<p>No surprises: what we commit to, we write down — and what we write down, we commit to. Last updated: November 2026.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section>
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>The written offer is the basis</h2>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				Every project starts with a written offer that states scope, price, timeline and risks before any commitment.
				The content on this website describes our launch-stage services; the details and terms of each service are
				finalized in the contract. Any change of scope after work begins goes through a written change request that is
				priced and approved before it is implemented.
			</p>

			<h2>Payment</h2>
			<ul class="steps-plain">
				<li>Small and medium projects: 50% upfront and 50% on delivery.</li>
				<li>Larger projects: milestone-based installments, defined in the written offer.</li>
				<li>For international clients, payment runs through the freelance platform's own milestone system.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Monthly subscription</h2>
			<ul class="steps-plain">
				<li>Optional for the first 30 days within the free support period after delivery, then agreed in writing.</li>
				<li>Covers operation monitoring, failure alerts and fixes, and small monthly changes within the plan's hour quota, with a monthly report of what the system did.</li>
				<li>Late monthly payment: support may be suspended after 15 days, and managed operation after 30 days, per the contract.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Third-party costs</h2>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				Hosting, domains, AI model usage, channel messaging fees and any external licenses are not included in the
				build price. They are set in writing in the offer: either on your own account directly, or within the
				subscription under a clear monthly cap.
			</p>

			<h2>Limits of responsibility</h2>
			<ul class="steps-plain">
				<li>We design every automation with a failure alert and a manual fallback plan, but we do not own or guarantee the continuity of external channels, electricity or the internet.</li>
				<li>Illustrative figures and examples on the website explain our method, are labelled as such, and are not a promise of a specific result; your results are measured from your own operation and written into your report.</li>
				<li>Prices and timelines mentioned on the website are indicative for the launch stage; what binds both sides is the signed written offer.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				For any material change, we update this page and note the date of the latest update at the top. Changes do not
				apply to existing contracts except by mutual agreement.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

</BaseEn>
